    <h2 id="audit-use">Using Reports for Audits</h2>

    <p>Gate reports are designed to serve directly as audit evidence. For security audits and compliance certifications:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Run <code>gate scan --verify</code> before generating a report -- active/inactive verification status demonstrates due diligence</li>
      <li>Use <code>gate report --format html</code> for a self-contained, shareable report with full styling</li>
      <li>Incident reports (generated via <code>gate report --incident &lt;id&gt;</code>) provide timelines and action logs suitable for breach documentation</li>
      <li>The audit log (<code>gate audit</code>) provides a tamper-evident chain of all Gate actions, verifiable with <code>gate audit --verify</code></li>
      <li>SARIF output uploaded to GitHub Code Scanning creates a persistent, versioned record of security findings tied to commits</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="info-box">
      <strong>Note:</strong> Gate's compliance mappings are informational. Consult your compliance team or a qualified auditor to confirm applicability to your specific certification requirements.
    </div>
